%N A114876 Let d(1)=1 and d(n) = d(n-1)*n^(2n-2)*(2n-1)^(3-2n). Then a(n)=numerator(d(n)).
%C A114876 Empirically coincides with the n-th monic Legendre polynomial discriminant numerator (A114877 is the denominator). - _Amit Lanis_, Sep 01 2026
%F A114876 a(n)/A114877(n) ~ A^3 * n^(n - 3/4) / (Pi * 2^(n^2 - 2*n + 1/12)), where A is the Glaisher-Kinkelin constant A074962. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 03 2026
%e A114876 1, 4/3, 108/125, 442368/2100875, 51200000/2977309629, 52428800000/118890080527911, ...
%t A114876 d[1] = 1; d[n_] := d[n] = d[n - 1]*n^(2 n - 2)*(2 n - 1)^(3 - 2 n); a[n_] := Numerator[d[n]]; Array[a, 10] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Mar 04 2023 *)
%Y A114876 Cf. A114877 (denominator).
